ract (if using). Line the bottom of your cake form with baking paper and grease the sides of the form. Preheat oven to 350°F (175°C). Incorporate 2 cups flour, 1 tsp baking powder, 1.5 cups almonds, 0.75 cup brown sugar, 2 tbsp melted butter, 2 pcs egg, 2 tbsp brandy, 5 drops almond extract, and 1 whole egg smoothly until evenly distributed."}]]}],["$","li","3",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Shape & Press Dough Evenly"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Cut 2/3 of the crust dough into slices and press down into the cake form. Cover the bottom of the cake form with the dough and bring the dough 2-3 cm (1 inch) up the sides of the form, pressing until even. Scoop the almond filling on top of the crust, spreading it evenly across the cake form. Roll out of the rest of the dough and slice into long strips. Lay the strips of dough across the cake in a grid. Don't worry of the strips break – simply press them back together on the cake."}]]}],["$","li","4",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Shape & Press Dough Evenly"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Gently brush the dough with egg wash. Bake for about 45 minutes. The top of the cake should be golden brown while the almond filling will remain soft."}]]}]]}],["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","cinnamon-roll-mug-cake",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/microwave-cinnamon-roll-mug-cake/","children":"Microwave Cinnamon Roll Mug Cake"}]}],["$","li","viral-9",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/3-milk-cloud-tres-leches-cake/","children":"3-Milk Cloud Tres Leches Cake"}]}],["$","li","viral-22",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/fluffy-japanese-souffl-jiggly-pancakes/","children":"Fluffy Japanese Soufflé Jiggly Pancakes"}]}],["$","li","viral-24",{"children":["$","a",null,{"href":"/recipes/red-velvet-cream-cheese-swirl-cake/","children":"Red Velvet Cream Cheese Swirl Cake"}]}],"$L13","$L14"]}]]}]}]
