e as fast."},{"stepNumber":2,"phaseLabel":"Build Flavor","title":"Preheat & Prep Your Pan","instructionTemplate":"Stir in the butter, egg, cognac and/or almond extract (if using). Line the bottom of your cake form with baking paper and grease the sides of the form. Preheat oven to 350°F (175°C). Incorporate {m53131_5}, {m53131_6}, {m53131_7}, {m53131_8}, {m53131_9}, {m53131_10}, {m53131_11}, {m53131_12}, and {m53131_13} smoothly until evenly distributed.","durationMin":3,"timerSeconds":180,"activeMeasureSummary":"Butter, Egg Yolks"},{"stepNumber":3,"phaseLabel":"Shape & Layer","title":"Shape & Press Dough Evenly","instructionTemplate":"Cut 2/3 of the crust dough into slices and press down into the cake form. Cover the bottom of the cake form with the dough and bring the dough 2-3 cm (1 inch) up the sides of the form, pressing until even. Scoop the almond filling on top of the crust, spreading it evenly across the cake form. Roll out of the rest of the dough and slice into long strips. Lay the strips of dough across the cake in a grid. Don't worry of the strips break – simply press them back together on the cake.","durationMin":3,"timerSeconds":180,"activeMeasureSummary":"Flour, Baking Powder"},{"stepNumber":4,"phaseLabel":"Bake / Chill","title":"Shape & Press Dough Evenly","instructionTemplate":"Gently brush the dough with egg wash. Bake for about 45 minutes. The top of the cake should be golden brown while the almond filling will remain soft.","durationMin":30,"timerSeconds":1800,"activeMeasureSummary":"Almonds, Brown Sugar","criticalTip":"Let set for 5–10 minutes before slicing or plating so the textures hold crisp and photogenic!","creatorSecret":"Wait until the sponge feels cool to the touch before frosting so your glaze or cream stays thick and glossy."}],"ugcQuotes":[{"id":"muq-53131","handle":"@baker_fyrsteka","image":"./ai-images/fyrstekake-norwegian-prince-cake.jpg","quote":"Followed the scaled metric steps—came out flawless in 45 mins!","rating":5}],"isHea